====================================================================================================
(0) THE LOSSES, THE PARSE AND THE FORMAT  [DESCRIPTIVE — and PREREG §6's rule]
====================================================================================================
PREREG §6's missing-cell rule, applied stage by stage. A cell lost at REJUDGE has
no before-state and leaves every table (it is the numerator of the feasibility
rate, and it is NOT a SOUND verdict with an empty list); lost at CONTEST it has an
unknown stance and is not a decline; lost at RULING it was contested and has no
after-state, and it is never counted as an uphold; lost at GRADE or at the
instrument it stays in P1-P3 and leaves that table alone. A retried cell is a
DIFFERENT DRAW and is never folded into a denominator.

