(1) P1 — DOES RECOURSE ON A DECOMPOSED JUDGMENT RAISE ACCURACY?  [PRIMARY]
====================================================================================================
Exact two-sided McNemar on before/after correctness, alpha = 0.05, PER ARM and
never pooled: F-weak's P1 and P2 are one intersection-union claim, and F-strong's
P1 is a separate family at its own alpha (PREREG §2's alpha policy).

BEFORE is the findings judge's OWN derived verdict (`initially_correct`) and not
jd3-M0's. Every fd1 arm is a rejudge, so the arm made its own decision; M0 is a
recorded comparator in section (4) and never P1's baseline. AFTER is
`final_correct`, and a cell nobody ruled on keeps the decision it had.

