====================================================================================================
  (4c) §3ac's IDENTITY, PER MECHANISM  [the bar P1 has to clear]
====================================================================================================
Recourse does not lower accuracy iff `f / b >= a / (1 - a)`, where `a` is the
accuracy of the decisions the mechanism SEES. Equivalently it hurts above the
break-even accuracy `a* = f / (f + b)` — and `f` and `b` there are RATES. The
derived verdict changes `a`, and therefore moves the bar, which is exactly why
this row is printed for every arm rather than left to the write-up.

mechanism                                     n        a   f = fix|wrong   b = break|right    f / b   a* = f/(f+b)     net
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
F-weak  (Maverick, both roles)             1067    62.8%           69.5%             38.7%     1.80          64.3%     +17
F-strong (luna, both roles)                 606    79.2%            5.6%              2.3%     2.42          70.8%      -4
jd5-B (the check arm)                       896    69.4%           52.6%             26.8%     1.96          66.2%     -23
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Read `f / b` against `a / (1 - a)` in the same row: the mechanism nets positive
only where the first exceeds the second. `a*` says the same thing as a threshold
on the first-instance accuracy.

====================================================================================================
  (4d) THE TWO RATES SPLIT BY BEFORE-VERDICT AND BY `findings_flaw_n`
====================================================================================================
PREREG §3 registers this split because the two directions are NOT symmetric under
a derived verdict, and jd5-B has no such asymmetry to compare against: breaking a
right SOUND verdict takes ONE upheld contest, and breaking a right FLAWED verdict
takes EVERY FLAW finding flipped. A break rate that is high on SOUND and near zero
on FLAWED is the derivation rule showing through, not the judge.

