====================================================================================================
  (4e) THE OBJECTION ITSELF — CONTESTS PER OBJECTION, BY KIND
====================================================================================================
Three kinds, and they are three different claims: a FINDING contest asks for the
opposite ruling on a numbered finding, an OMISSION says the list missed a flaw the
record raised, a CONTRADICTION says two findings say the same thing and were ruled
differently. The mix is what the decomposition bought, and it has no counterpart
in jd3-jd6, where the objection was the whole judgment.

