====================================================================================================
  (4f) VALIDITY, BY KIND AND BY `label_basis`  [NEVER POOLED ACROSS THE TWO]
====================================================================================================
PREREG §5(a): on FLAWED items 'a real flaw' is operationalised as THE ANNOTATED
flaw, so a NOT A FLAW -> FLAW contest on a genuine but unannotated error is
INVALID BY RULE — validity on flawed items is a LOWER BOUND — while its mirror
FLAW -> NOT A FLAW is VALID by rule, an UPPER bound. The two are never averaged
together, and `label_basis` is where that split lives.

