====================================================================================================
  (4g) THE RULING — LINE/PROSE MISMATCH, EMPTY PROSE, AND THE APPENDED FINDINGS
====================================================================================================
`ruling_line_mismatch` is the instrument that keeps `changed_the_decision`
falsifiable: Haiku reads the ruling's PROSE and says whether it supports every
line. `ruling_leadin_stripped` is a fact about the RULING PROMPT and not the
reader — two of three findings-reader mismatches in the smoke were a dangling
lead-in ('The final ruling for Contest 1 is:') that the strip dropped — so the
two are printed together and the mismatch rate is read with the lead-in count.

